<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ming Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ming Dynasty, Ming dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ming Empire was the Chinese dynasty founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a> in 1368 after the expulsion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>. It rebuilt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-wall-of-china">Great Wall</a>, launched the treasure voyages of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-he">Zheng He</a> and became a centre of global <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> trade. It fell in 1644 to rebellion and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> conquest, which founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ming-empire.jpg" alt="Ming Empire" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albert Herrmann Creator:Q1509115 &amp;amp; Georg Westermann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Ming_Chinese_empire_1415_(cropped_2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
